  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>ACTA (Amicale du Chien de Travail d'Antibes) is a dog club based in the 3 Moulins zone in Antibes. The City of Antibes Juan-les-Pins association directory lists four activities for it: training, ring, agility and obedience.</p>
      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>The club is listed by the Société Centrale Canine as an approved club (no. 2812), with a ground at the ZI des 3 Moulins, 63 route des Alisiers, in Antibes, the address also given by the City's directory. It is active: it held a ring trial on 18/04/2026, which appears in the official 2026 ring trial calendar, and that calendar also gives its e-mail address, act.antibes@gmail.com. The City's directory links to no club website; the phone number it publishes is the president's and is not reproduced here, so e-mail is the contact method used.</p>
      <p><strong>Worth checking before you go:</strong> session times, enrolment conditions and fees are not published; what the training classes cover for a non-sport dog should therefore be confirmed by e-mail.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: write to the club before coming to find out session times and whether your dog can follow a training class.</div>
      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The ground is in the 3 Moulins industrial zone, route des Alisiers: plan to drive, then head to Cap d'Antibes and its coastal paths to extend your outing.</p>
